ENGLISH VERSION (courtesy translation — the French version prevails)
================================================================================

1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means the source code, configuration files, database schemas,
   migrations, email templates, assets and documentation contained in this
   repository, together with any earlier or later version released by the
   Holder.

   "Holder" means Thibault JEANPIERRE, author and sole owner of the economic
   rights in the Software.

   "You" means any individual or legal entity accessing the Software.

2. NATURE OF THE PUBLICATION

   The Software is published as "source-available": its code is made publicly
   readable. This publication is NOT an open source release and grants NO
   transfer of rights. Making the code publicly visible does not waive the
   Holder's copyright, nor does it imply any licence to use it.

3. RIGHTS GRANTED

   The Holder grants You a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence,
   revocable at any time, strictly limited to:

   a) viewing and reading the source code;
   b) performing a technical or security audit of the code;
   c) evaluating the Software for professional or educational assessment,
      including running it locally on a strictly personal and temporary basis;
   d) quoting short excerpts of the code for analysis, teaching, criticism or
      vulnerability reporting, provided the source and the Holder are cited.

4. RESTRICTIONS

   Without the Holder's prior express written permission, You may NOT:

   a) operate the Software in production, for yourself or for a third party;
   b) copy, reproduce, duplicate or fork the Software, in whole or in part,
      beyond what is strictly necessary under Section 3;
   c) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the Software;
   d) distribute, publish, sublicense, rent, lend, sell or resell it;
   e) commercially exploit the Software in any form, including SaaS, hosted,
      managed or white-label offerings;
   f) use the Software, in whole or in part, to design, train or improve a
      competing product or service;
   g) use the Software as training data for a machine learning model;
   h) remove, obscure or alter any copyright, licence, authorship notice or
      trade mark appearing in the Software.

   This Section applies without prejudice to mandatory exceptions granted by
   applicable law, in particular the right to decompile for interoperability
   purposes.

5. CONTRIBUTIONS

   The Software is developed and maintained exclusively by the Holder. No
   external contribution is solicited or accepted. Any contribution
   nonetheless submitted (pull request, patch, code suggestion) is deemed
   offered to the Holder free of charge, with an irrevocable worldwide
   assignment of all related economic rights, with no obligation for the
   Holder to merge or acknowledge it.

   Vulnerability reports, however, are welcome and must be sent privately to
   the Holder (see SECURITY in the README).

6. TRADE MARKS

   "AeroConnect", its logo and associated visual identity remain the property
   of the Holder. This licence grants no right to use those distinctive signs.

7. COMMERCIAL LICENCE

   Any use beyond Section 3 — in particular deployment within a flying club
   or ULM club — requires a separate commercial licence negotiated directly
   with the Holder.

8. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

   The Software relies on third-party libraries distributed under their own
   licences (see package.json and the node_modules directory). This licence
   applies only to the original elements of the Software and does not alter
   the rights and obligations attached to those third-party components.

9. TERMINATION

   The rights granted in Section 3 terminate automatically, without notice,
   upon any breach of Section 4. You must then cease all use of the Software
   and destroy every copy in Your possession. The Holder further reserves the
   right to revoke those rights at any time and to change the terms applying
   to future versions.

10. NO WARRANTY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AVAILABILITY, ACCURACY AND
   NON-INFRINGEMENT.

   The Software includes features related to aviation safety (flight logbook,
   maintenance tracking, pilot ratings). It is in no way a substitute for
   applicable regulatory obligations, nor for the judgement of the pilot in
   command, the technical manager or the club's management.

11. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

   TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE HOLDER SHALL NOT BE
   LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT OR INDIRECT DAMAGES, TANGIBLE OR INTANGIBLE, LOSS OF
   DATA, LOSS OF BUSINESS OR ANY OTHER HARM ARISING FROM THE USE OF, OR
   INABILITY TO USE, THE SOFTWARE.

12. GOVERNING LAW

   This licence is governed by French law. Any dispute relating to its
   validity, interpretation or performance falls within the exclusive
   jurisdiction of the French courts, subject to mandatory jurisdiction rules
   applicable to consumers.
